  "body": "## Status\n\nIndependent proof-step audit; no new \u03ba, decoder construction, supplier, or selected-frontier change. This is a second review following the completed claim [#1275](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1275) and [PR #1292](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1292). It does not repeat the tangent-matrix census: it checks the local regularity implication and exhaustively verifies the displayed P104 kernel generators against the pinned reduced systems.\n\n## Finding\n\nFor each of the three P104 representatives, the pinned certificate gives tangent dimension 103 at `K0 = 2G`, equal to the dimension of the diagonal-torus orbit `O`. Since `O` is smooth and contained in the masked rank-eight variety `X`, `dim_K0(X) >= 103`; the certified tangent dimension gives `dim(T_K0 X) <= 103`. Thus the local ring is regular and `X` is smooth near `K0`. The inclusion `O -> X` has an isomorphism on tangent spaces between smooth 103-dimensional manifolds, so the inverse function theorem gives equality of their germs.\n\nThis supports the stated **local** conclusion. It does not rule out distant off-orbit P104 components or rank-nine costly parts and does not change the selected \u03ba.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/seed38-p104-orbit-regularity-audit/verify.py\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/seed38-p104-orbit-regularity-audit --check-only\n```\n\nThe verifier replays the pinned PR #1292 certificate, including its D4\u2295D4 negative control and seeded sample, then checks all 168 gauge/torus generators against all 4,992 reduced rows in each of the three P104 classes modulo `2^31 - 1`. It reports tangent/orbit dimension 103. The proof argument is in `PROOF.md`.\n\n## Pins and attribution\n\n- Base: `bce54fb3f895cbe5cd4c0eb477c3afeed100190f`.\n- Audited source: PR #1292 head `7a8325f6c8e5a6830ce919965a2959ac459e010a`; source files and base provenance files are SHA-256/Git-blob pinned in `SOURCES.json`.\n- Local replay ran on Python 3.14.7 because Python 3.12 is not installed here; the package manifest registers the standard-library replay for the repository's Python 3.12 runner.\n- Credit Navinor (with opencode assistance) for PR #1292; DreamingOfClouds for PR #717's mask model; themilkman216 for PR #968's frame-pair floor; and burntout76 for PR #1212's P112/P120 rigidity. This package was prepared with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance; no independent human review is claimed.\n",
